        "ai_explanation": "A compliance assessment of the Source of Wealth (SoW) documentation for Adrian Wong Kok Leong was conducted in relation to an onboarding portfolio exposure of MYR 2,400,000. The customer declared an annual net income of MYR 180,000 derived from employment at Apex Meridian Technologies Sdn. Bhd. However, transactional analysis identified total bank deposits of MYR 3,600,000 over a 12-month period. This demonstrates an observed deposit-to-salary ratio of 20.00x, substantially breaching our institutional compliance benchmark threshold of <= 1.25x.\n\nThe substantial discrepancy between the customer's declared employment earnings and the documented inflows of MYR 3,600,000 constitutes a severe compliance violation. In accordance with AML/CFT regulatory mandates and Shariah-compliant wealth verification standards, wealth managers must establish unambiguous, legitimate, and fully substantiated origin of funds. The verified inflows exceed the declared income by over 200% without corresponding secondary documentation, such as asset sale deeds or audited tax returns, creating an unmitigated risk of illicit or unverified capital injection.\n\nConsequently, the customer profile has triggered a Critical Income-Deposit Discrepancy flag, yielding a Risk Score of 50/100 and an overall Risk Level of CRITICAL. Due to the failure to satisfy the deposit-to-income verification rule and the presence of critical financial inconsistencies, the compliance determination for this application is formal REJECTED."
      }
